        "proof_strategy": "direct",
        "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice. Let $M$ be the interior of a compact connected orientable three-manifold with $k\\ge1$ torus cusps and a complete finite-volume hyperbolic metric. Choose a peripheral basis $(\\mu_i,\\lambda_i)$ on each cusp. On the augmented holonomy space obtained by selecting one common invariant line on each peripheral subgroup, near the complete structure write $u_i$ and $v_i$ for the logarithms of the eigenvalue ratios of the peripheral holonomies of $\\mu_i$ and $\\lambda_i$, with branches chosen so $u_i=v_i=0$ at the complete structure. There is a neighborhood of the complete point in the $k$ generalized parameter spheres such that primitive integral filling data $(p_i,q_i)$ in that neighborhood satisfying $p_i u_i+q_i v_i=2\\pi i$ at every filled cusp produce a complete finite-volume hyperbolic structure on the ordinary filled manifold. The peripheral full-turn equations are solved simultaneously across the $k$ cusps; unfilled cusps retain their complete parabolic holonomy. No universal numeric length threshold is asserted."
